# Autobot: number words for the Kokoro voice (autobot/shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/wckdboy/autobot/shared/tts/EnglishNumbers.kt)
{"id": "autobot-cardinal-2340", "tags": ["autobot", "code-reading"], "system": "Answer with the result only, no explanation.", "prompt": "Autobot's text-to-speech front end spells numbers like this (Kotlin):\n\n```kotlin\n    private val ones = listOf(\n        \"zero\", \"one\", \"two\", \"three\", \"four\", \"five\", \"six\", \"seven\", \"eight\", \"nine\", \"ten\",\n        \"eleven\", \"twelve\", \"thirteen\", \"fourteen\", \"fifteen\", \"sixteen\", \"seventeen\", \"eighteen\", \"nineteen\",\n    )\n    private val tens = listOf(\"\", \"\", \"twenty\", \"thirty\", \"forty\", \"fifty\", \"sixty\", \"seventy\", \"eighty\", \"ninety\")\n    private val scales = listOf(\"\", \"thousand\", \"million\", \"billion\", \"trillion\", \"quadrillion\", \"quintillion\")\n    private val ords = mapOf(\n        \"one\" to \"first\", \"two\" to \"second\", \"three\" to \"third\", \"four\" to \"fourth\", \"five\" to \"fifth\", \"six\" to \"sixth\",\n        \"seven\" to \"seventh\", \"eight\" to \"eighth\", \"nine\" to \"ninth\", \"ten\" to \"tenth\", \"eleven\" to \"eleventh\", \"twelve\" to \"twelfth\",\n    )\n\n    private fun belowHundred(n: Int): String = if (n < 20) ones[n] else tens[n / 10] + if (n % 10 != 0) \"-\" + ones[n % 10] else \"\"\n\n    private fun belowThousand(n: Int): String = when {\n        n < 100 -> belowHundred(n)\n        n % 100 == 0 -> ones[n / 100] + \" hundred\"\n        else -> ones[n / 100] + \" hundred and \" + belowHundred(n % 100)\n    }\n\n    // Unsigned inside: -Long.MIN_VALUE is itself negative.\n    fun cardinal(value: Long): String = if (value < 0) \"minus \" + cardinal(0uL - value.toULong()) else cardinal(value.toULong())\n\n    private fun cardinal(value: ULong): String {\n        if (value == 0uL) return \"zero\"\n        val groups = mutableListOf<Int>()\n        var v = value\n        while (v > 0uL) {\n            groups += (v % 1000uL).toInt()\n            v /= 1000uL\n        }\n        val parts = mutableListOf<String>()\n        for (i in groups.indices.reversed()) {\n            val g = groups[i]\n            if (g == 0) continue\n            parts += belowThousand(g) + if (i > 0) \" \" + scales[i] else \"\"\n        }\n        // num2words joins a trailing group under a hundred with \"and\", others with \", \".\n        val last = groups[0]\n        return if (parts.size > 1 && last in 1..99) parts.dropLast(1).joinToString(\", \") + \" and \" + parts.last() else parts.joinToString(\", \")\n    }\n```\n\nWhat exact string does `cardinal(2340L)` return? Answer with the string only, without quotes.", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "^[\\\"`]?two thousand, three hundred and forty[\\\"`]?\\.?$"}], "max_tokens": 1200}
{"id": "autobot-ordinal-42", "tags": ["autobot", "code-reading"], "system": "Answer with the result only, no explanation.", "prompt": "Autobot's text-to-speech front end (Kotlin):\n\n```kotlin\n    private val ords = mapOf(\n        \"one\" to \"first\", \"two\" to \"second\", \"three\" to \"third\", \"four\" to \"fourth\", \"five\" to \"fifth\", \"six\" to \"sixth\",\n        \"seven\" to \"seventh\", \"eight\" to \"eighth\", \"nine\" to \"ninth\", \"ten\" to \"tenth\", \"eleven\" to \"eleventh\", \"twelve\" to \"twelfth\",\n    )\n\n    // cardinal(42L) returns \"forty-two\"\n    fun ordinal(value: Long): String {\n        val words = cardinal(value).split(' ').toMutableList()\n        val pieces = words.last().split('-').toMutableList()\n        val last = pieces.last()\n        pieces[pieces.size - 1] = ords[last] ?: ((if (last.endsWith(\"y\")) last.dropLast(1) + \"ie\" else last) + \"th\")\n        words[words.size - 1] = pieces.joinToString(\"-\")\n        return words.joinToString(\" \")\n    }\n```\n\nWhat exact string does `ordinal(42L)` return? Answer with the string only, without quotes.", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "^[\\\"`]?forty-second[\\\"`]?\\.?$"}], "max_tokens": 800}
