{"id": "autobot-loopback-urls", "tags": ["autobot", "code-reading"], "system": "Answer with JSON only.", "prompt": "Autobot decides which URLs stay on the device (Kotlin):\n\n```kotlin\nobject Loopback {\n    private val ipv4Loopback = Regex(\"^127(\\\\.(25[0-5]|2[0-4]\\\\d|1?\\\\d?\\\\d)){3}$\")\n\n    fun isLoopback(host: String?): Boolean {\n        if (host.isNullOrBlank()) return false\n        val h = host.trim().lowercase().removePrefix(\"[\").removeSuffix(\"]\")\n        return h == \"localhost\" ||\n            h.endsWith(\".localhost\") ||\n            h == \"::1\" ||\n            h == \"0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1\" ||\n            h == EMULATOR_HOST ||\n            ipv4Loopback.matches(h)\n    }\n\n    /** Extracts the host part of a URL string without resolving it. */\n    fun isLoopbackUrl(url: String?): Boolean {\n        if (url.isNullOrBlank()) return false\n        val afterScheme = url.substringAfter(\"://\", url)\n        val authority = afterScheme.substringBefore('/').substringAfterLast('@')\n        val host = if (authority.startsWith(\"[\")) {\n            authority.substringBefore(']') + \"]\"\n        } else {\n            authority.substringBefore(':')\n        }\n        return isLoopback(host)\n    }\n\n    const val EMULATOR_HOST = \"10.0.2.2\"\n}\n```\n\nFor each URL, does `isLoopbackUrl` return true?\na) http://user@localhost:8080/x\nb) http://localhost.evil.com/\nc) http://127.0.0.256/\nd) http://[::1]:11434/\ne) http://10.0.2.2:8080\n\nAnswer as {\"a\": bool, \"b\": bool, \"c\": bool, \"d\": bool, \"e\": bool}.", "checks": [{"type": "json", "path": "a", "equals": true}, {"type": "json", "path": "b", "equals": false}, {"type": "json", "path": "c", "equals": false}, {"type": "json", "path": "d", "equals": true}, {"type": "json", "path": "e", "equals": true}], "max_tokens": 1500}
{"id": "autobot-loopback-bug", "tags": ["autobot", "bug-finding"], "system": "Answer with the number only.", "prompt": "This Kotlin function must return true only for hosts that never leave the device: `localhost`, any subdomain of `localhost` (such as `api.localhost`), IPv6 `::1`, the emulator alias and 127.x.x.x. One line lets a remote host through. Which line number is the bug?\n\n```kotlin\n1  fun isLoopback(host: String?): Boolean {\n2      if (host.isNullOrBlank()) return false\n3      val h = host.trim().lowercase().removePrefix(\"[\").removeSuffix(\"]\")\n4      return h == \"localhost\" ||\n5          h.endsWith(\"localhost\") ||\n6          h == \"::1\" ||\n7          h == \"0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1\" ||\n8          h == EMULATOR_HOST ||\n9          ipv4Loopback.matches(h)\n10 }\n```", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "(?i)^[`*]*(line\\s*)?5[`*]*\\.?$"}], "max_tokens": 800}
{"id": "autobot-glob-doublestar", "tags": ["autobot", "code-reading"], "system": "Answer with JSON only.", "prompt": "Autobot's agent matches workspace files with this glob (Kotlin; the rest of `toRegex` handles `[...]` and `\\\\` escapes):\n\n```kotlin\nclass Glob(pattern: String) {\n    private val regex = Regex(toRegex(pattern))\n\n    fun matches(path: String): Boolean = regex.matches(path)\n\n    private companion object {\n        fun toRegex(glob: String): String {\n            val out = StringBuilder()\n            var i = 0\n            var inGroup = false\n            while (i < glob.length) {\n                val c = glob[i]\n                when {\n                    c == '*' && glob.getOrNull(i + 1) == '*' -> {\n                        out.append(\".*\")\n                        i++\n                    }\n                    c == '*' -> out.append(\"[^/]*\")\n                    c == '?' -> out.append(\"[^/]\")\n                    c == '{' && !inGroup -> {\n                        out.append(\"(?:\")\n                        inGroup = true\n                    }\n                    c == '}' && inGroup -> {\n                        out.append(')')\n                        inGroup = false\n                    }\n                    c == ',' && inGroup -> out.append('|')\n                    // ... character classes ([...], [!...]) and backslash escapes ...\n                    else -> out.append(Regex.escape(c.toString()))\n                }\n                i++\n            }\n            return out.toString()\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWith `val g = Glob(\"**/*.kt\")`, what are `g.matches(\"Main.kt\")` and `g.matches(\"src/app/Main.kt\")`? Answer as {\"first\": bool, \"second\": bool}.", "checks": [{"type": "json", "path": "first", "equals": false}, {"type": "json", "path": "second", "equals": true}], "max_tokens": 1500}
