{"id": "omnie-schedule-90m", "tags": ["omnie", "code-reading", "typescript"], "system": "Answer with JSON only.", "prompt": "From omnie-cli (TypeScript):\n\n```ts\nfunction parseRecurrence(text: string): Recurrence {\n  const lowered = text.toLowerCase();\n  switch (lowered) {\n    case \"hourly\":\n      return { kind: \"hourly\" };\n    case \"daily\":\n      return { kind: \"daily\" };\n    case \"weekly\":\n      return { kind: \"weekly\" };\n    default:\n      break;\n  }\n  const every = /^every:(\\d+)$/.exec(lowered);\n  if (every?.[1] !== undefined) return { kind: \"every\", seconds: requireInterval(Number(every[1]), text) };\n  const unit = /^(\\d+)(s|m|h)$/.exec(lowered);\n  if (unit?.[1] !== undefined && unit[2] !== undefined) {\n    const amount = Number(unit[1]);\n    const seconds = unit[2] === \"s\" ? amount : unit[2] === \"m\" ? amount * 60 : amount * 3600;\n    return { kind: \"every\", seconds: requireInterval(seconds, text) };\n  }\n  throw new UsageError(\n    `--schedule must be hourly, daily, weekly, a duration like 15m, or every:120. Received ${JSON.stringify(text)}.`,\n  );\n}\n\nfunction requireInterval(seconds: number, text: string): number {\n  if (!Number.isFinite(seconds) || seconds < 60) {\n    throw new UsageError(`Schedule interval must be at least 60 seconds. Received ${JSON.stringify(text)}.`);\n  }\n  return seconds;\n}\n```\n\nWhat does `parseRecurrence(\"90m\")` return? Answer with the object as JSON.", "checks": [{"type": "json", "path": "kind", "equals": "every"}, {"type": "json", "path": "seconds", "equals": 5400}], "max_tokens": 800}
