{"id": "nightfall-expr-sin-unit", "tags": ["nightfall", "code-reading", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with the result only, no explanation.", "prompt": "Nightfall's expression evaluator, function calls (C++). `30` is a dimensionless scalar; `30 deg` is an angle.\n\n```cpp\n      const auto b = pop();\n      q = b;\n      if (op.kind == K::kNeg)\n        q.value = -b.value;\n      else if (op.kind == K::kFunc) {\n        if (op.text == \"sqrt\") {\n          const auto d = powered(b.dimension, 0.5);\n          if (!d) return fail(\"unit\", \"sqrt requires even dimension powers\");\n          q.dimension = *d;\n        } else if (op.text != \"abs\") {\n          const bool trig = op.text == \"sin\" || op.text == \"cos\" || op.text == \"tan\";\n          if (b.dimension != (trig ? kAngle : kScalar))\n            return fail(\"unit\", op.text + (trig ? \" requires an angle\" : \" requires a scalar\"));\n          q.dimension =\n              op.text == \"asin\" || op.text == \"acos\" || op.text == \"atan\" ? kAngle : kScalar;\n        }\n        q.value = math::Expression::apply_function(op.text, b.value);\n```\n\nEvaluating `sin(30)` fails. What is the exact error message? Answer with the message only.", "checks": [{"type": "contains", "value": "sin requires an angle"}, {"type": "max_words", "value": 12}], "max_tokens": 600}
# Nightfall: tolerances and vectors (nightfall/core/math/include/nf/math/tolerance.hpp, vec.hpp)
{"id": "nightfall-near", "tags": ["nightfall", "code-reading", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with the result only, no explanation.", "prompt": "From Nightfall's math library (C++):\n\n```cpp\n/// Tolerances used by every geometric comparison in Nightfall.\n///\n/// Lengths are millimetres and angles are radians, everywhere. No comparison in `core/`\n/// may use a bare epsilon; it takes a `Tolerance` (or one of its fields) instead.\nstruct Tolerance {\n  /// Two points closer than this are the same point (mm).\n  double linear = 1e-6;\n  /// Two directions closer than this are the same direction (rad).\n  double angular = 1e-9;\n\n  [[nodiscard]] static constexpr Tolerance standard() noexcept { return {}; }\n};\n\n/// |value|, usable in constant expressions.\n[[nodiscard]] constexpr double abs(double value) noexcept { return value < 0.0 ? -value : value; }\n\n/// True when `a` and `b` differ by at most `tolerance` (absolute).\n[[nodiscard]] constexpr bool near(double a, double b, double tolerance) noexcept {\n  return abs(a - b) <= tolerance;\n}\n```\n\nWhat does `near(1.0, 1.0000005, Tolerance::standard().linear)` return? Answer true or false.", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "(?i)^[`*]*true[`*]*\\.?$"}], "max_tokens": 500}
{"id": "nightfall-normalized-tiny", "tags": ["nightfall", "code-reading", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with the result only, no explanation.", "prompt": "From Nightfall's math library (C++). `Tolerance::standard().linear` is 1e-6 mm.\n\n```cpp\n/// Unit vector in the direction of `a`, or nothing if `a` is shorter than `tol.linear`\n/// (its direction is not meaningful) or has a NaN or infinite component.\n[[nodiscard]] inline std::optional<Vec2> normalized(\n    Vec2 a, Tolerance tol = Tolerance::standard()) noexcept {\n  double len = length(a);\n  if (!(len > tol.linear)) return std::nullopt;  // also rejects NaN\n  if (std::isinf(len)) {\n    // The length overflowed: rescale by the largest component, which is exact enough.\n    const double largest = std::fmax(abs(a.x), abs(a.y));\n    if (!std::isfinite(largest)) return std::nullopt;\n    a = a / largest;\n    len = length(a);\n  }\n  return a / len;\n}\n```\n\nDoes `normalized(Vec2{5e-7, 0.0})` return a value? Answer yes or no.", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "(?i)^[`*]*no[`*]*\\.?$"}], "max_tokens": 500}
{"id": "nightfall-cross-bug", "tags": ["nightfall", "bug-finding", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with the number only.", "prompt": "This C++ from a geometry kernel has one wrong line: the cross product must follow the right-hand rule, so cross({1,0,0}, {0,1,0}) = {0,0,1} and cross({0,0,1}, {1,0,0}) = {0,1,0}. Which line number is wrong?\n\n```cpp\n1 [[nodiscard]] constexpr double dot(Vec3 a, Vec3 b) noexcept {\n2   return a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y + a.z * b.z;\n3 }\n4 [[nodiscard]] constexpr Vec3 cross(Vec3 a, Vec3 b) noexcept {\n5   return {a.y * b.z - a.z * b.y,\n6           a.x * b.z - a.z * b.x,\n7           a.x * b.y - a.y * b.x};\n8 }\n9 [[nodiscard]] constexpr double length_squared(Vec3 a) noexcept { return dot(a, a); }\n```", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "(?i)^[`*]*(line\\s*)?6[`*]*\\.?$"}], "max_tokens": 1000}
{"id": "nightfall-cpp-cosine", "tags": ["nightfall", "coding", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with the code only, no explanation.", "prompt": "Nightfall's math library has `double dot(Vec3 a, Vec3 b)` and `double length(Vec3 a)`. Write one C++ expression for the cosine of the angle between the non-zero vectors `a` and `b`, using only those two functions.", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "dot\\(\\s*a\\s*,\\s*b\\s*\\)\\s*/\\s*\\(\\s*length\\(\\s*a\\s*\\)\\s*\\*\\s*length\\(\\s*b\\s*\\)\\s*\\)"}], "max_tokens": 300}
# Nightfall: NURBS knot vectors (nightfall/core/math/src/knot_vector.cpp)
{"id": "nightfall-knots-uniform", "tags": ["nightfall", "code-reading", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with JSON only.", "prompt": "From Nightfall's NURBS library (C++):\n\n```cpp\nKnotVector KnotVector::uniform_clamped(int degree, int control_points) {\n  if (degree < 1 || degree > kMaxDegree) {\n    throw std::invalid_argument(\"uniform_clamped: degree must be 1..kMaxDegree\");\n  }\n  if (control_points < degree + 1) {\n    throw std::invalid_argument(\"uniform_clamped: need at least degree + 1 control points\");\n  }\n  std::vector<double> k;\n  const int interior = control_points - degree - 1;\n  k.insert(k.end(), static_cast<std::size_t>(degree + 1), 0.0);\n  for (int i = 1; i <= interior; ++i) k.push_back(static_cast<double>(i) / (interior + 1));\n  k.insert(k.end(), static_cast<std::size_t>(degree + 1), 1.0);\n  auto made = make(std::move(k), degree);\n  if (!made) throw std::invalid_argument(\"uniform_clamped: \" + made.error());\n  return *made;\n}\n```\n\nWhat knots does `KnotVector::uniform_clamped(2, 4)` hold? Answer as {\"knots\": [numbers]}.", "checks": [{"type": "json", "path": "knots.0", "equals": 0}, {"type": "json", "path": "knots.1", "equals": 0}, {"type": "json", "path": "knots.2", "equals": 0}, {"type": "json", "path": "knots.3", "equals": 0.5}, {"type": "json", "path": "knots.4", "equals": 1}, {"type": "json", "path": "knots.5", "equals": 1}, {"type": "json", "path": "knots.6", "equals": 1}, {"type": "not_contains", "value": "0.33"}], "max_tokens": 1500}
{"id": "nightfall-find-span", "tags": ["nightfall", "code-reading", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with the number only.", "prompt": "From Nightfall's NURBS library (C++). The knot vector is k = [0, 0, 0, 0.5, 1, 1, 1] with degree 2, so `control_point_count()` is 4.\n\n```cpp\nint KnotVector::find_span(double u) const noexcept {\n  const std::vector<double>& k = *knots_;\n  const int n = control_point_count() - 1;\n  if (u >= k[static_cast<std::size_t>(n + 1)]) return n;  // end of domain -> last span\n  if (u <= k[static_cast<std::size_t>(degree_)]) return degree_;\n  int low = degree_, high = n + 1;\n  int mid = (low + high) / 2;\n  while (u < k[static_cast<std::size_t>(mid)] || u >= k[static_cast<std::size_t>(mid + 1)]) {\n    if (u < k[static_cast<std::size_t>(mid)]) {\n      high = mid;\n    } else {\n      low = mid;\n    }\n    mid = (low + high) / 2;\n  }\n  return mid;\n}\n```\n\nWhat does `find_span(0.25)` return?", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "^[`*]*2[`*]*\\.?$"}], "max_tokens": 1500}
{"id": "nightfall-knot-error", "tags": ["nightfall", "code-reading", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with the result only, no explanation.", "prompt": "From Nightfall's NURBS library (C++; `multiplicity_at(k, i)` counts how many knots from index i on equal k[i]; kMaxDegree is 9):\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected<KnotVector, std::string> KnotVector::make(std::vector<double> knots, int degree) {\n  if (degree < 1 || degree > kMaxDegree) {\n    return std::unexpected(\"degree must be in [1, \" + std::to_string(kMaxDegree) + \"]\");\n  }\n  const auto p = static_cast<std::size_t>(degree);\n  if (knots.size() < 2 * (p + 1)) {\n    return std::unexpected(\"need at least 2(p + 1) knots\");\n  }\n  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < knots.size(); ++i) {\n    if (!std::isfinite(knots[i])) return std::unexpected(\"knots must be finite\");\n    if (i > 0 && knots[i] < knots[i - 1]) return std::unexpected(\"knots must be non-decreasing\");\n  }\n  if (multiplicity_at(knots, 0) != p + 1) {\n    return std::unexpected(\"first knot must have multiplicity p + 1 (clamped)\");\n  }\n  if (multiplicity_at(knots, knots.size() - p - 1) != p + 1 ||\n      knots[knots.size() - p - 2] == knots.back()) {\n    return std::unexpected(\"last knot must have multiplicity p + 1 (clamped)\");\n  }\n  if (!(knots[p] < knots[knots.size() - p - 1])) return std::unexpected(\"empty domain\");\n  for (std::size_t i = p + 1; i < knots.size() - p - 1;) {\n    const std::size_t m = multiplicity_at(knots, i);\n    if (m > p) return std::unexpected(\"interior knot multiplicity must be <= p\");\n    i += m;\n  }\n```\n\nWhich error message does `KnotVector::make({0, 0, 0, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 1, 1, 1}, 2)` return? Answer with the message only.", "checks": [{"type": "contains", "value": "interior knot multiplicity must be <= p"}, {"type": "max_words", "value": 12}], "max_tokens": 1500}
# Nightfall: part parameters (nightfall/core/ir/src/parameters.cpp, docs/rfcs/0005-feature-ir.md)
{"id": "nightfall-param-ids", "tags": ["nightfall", "code-reading", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with JSON only.", "prompt": "Nightfall checks parameter IDs with this C++:\n\n```cpp\nbool identifier(std::string_view s) {\n  const auto letter = [](char c) { return (c >= 'a' && c <= 'z') || c == '_'; };\n  return !s.empty() && s.size() <= 64 && letter(s.front()) &&\n         std::ranges::all_of(s, [&](char c) { return letter(c) || (c >= '0' && c <= '9'); });\n}\n```\n\nFor each ID, is it valid?\na) \"Bolt_d\"\nb) \"_wall2\"\nc) \"2wall\"\nd) \"hole-d\"\n\nAnswer as {\"a\": bool, \"b\": bool, \"c\": bool, \"d\": bool}.", "checks": [{"type": "json", "path": "a", "equals": false}, {"type": "json", "path": "b", "equals": true}, {"type": "json", "path": "c", "equals": false}, {"type": "json", "path": "d", "equals": false}], "max_tokens": 1000}
{"id": "nightfall-param-hole", "tags": ["nightfall", "engineering", "extraction"], "system": "Answer with the number only.", "prompt": "A Nightfall part (feature IR, lengths in mm):\n\n```json\n  \"params\": [\n    { \"name\": \"width\", \"value\": \"40 mm\", \"min\": \"10 mm\", \"max\": \"200 mm\", \"doc\": \"Overall width\" },\n    { \"name\": \"wall\", \"value\": \"3 mm\" },\n    { \"name\": \"hole_d\", \"value\": \"wall * 1.7\" }\n  ],\n```\n\nParameters resolve in dependency order. What is `hole_d` in mm?", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "^[`*]*5\\.10*[`*]*\\.?$"}], "max_tokens": 500}
{"id": "nightfall-param-cycle", "tags": ["nightfall", "code-reading", "cpp"], "system": "Answer with the result only, no explanation.", "prompt": "Nightfall orders parameters with this C++ (`fields_[i][0]->dependencies` lists the parameter indices that parameter i's value uses, and `fail` records the message):\n\n```cpp\n  std::vector<std::size_t> topological_order() {\n    struct Frame {\n      std::size_t id, next = 0;\n    };\n    std::vector<Frame> stack;\n    std::vector<std::size_t> positions(params_.size()), order;\n    std::vector<char> state(params_.size(), 0);\n    for (std::size_t root = 0; root < params_.size(); ++root) {\n      if (state[root] != 0) continue;\n      state[root] = 1;\n      positions[root] = 0;\n      stack.push_back({root});\n      while (!stack.empty()) {\n        auto& frame = stack.back();\n        const auto& dependencies = fields_[frame.id][0]->dependencies;\n        if (frame.next == dependencies.size()) {\n          state[frame.id] = 2;\n          order.push_back(frame.id);\n          stack.pop_back();\n          continue;\n        }\n        const auto d = dependencies[frame.next++];\n        if (state[d] == 2) continue;\n        if (state[d] == 1) {\n          if (errors_.size() < 128) {\n            std::string message = \"parameter cycle: \";\n            const auto end = std::min(stack.size(), positions[d] + 64);\n            for (auto k = positions[d]; k < end; ++k) message += params_[stack[k].id].name + \" -> \";\n            if (end < stack.size()) message += \"... -> \";\n            fail(\"cycle\", message + params_[d].name, at(frame.id, \"value\"));\n          }\n          continue;\n        }\n        positions[d] = stack.size();\n        state[d] = 1;\n        stack.push_back({d});\n      }\n    }\n    return order;\n  }\n```\n\nThe parameters are, in order: index 0 `a` with value \"b + 1 mm\", index 1 `b` with value \"a * 2\". What message is recorded? Answer with the message only.", "checks": [{"type": "regex", "pattern": "parameter cycle: a -> b -> a\\b"}], "max_tokens": 2000}
